//? Title: Independent multi-label learning on actual COCO photographs
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
One photograph can contain several annotated categories. Stable weighted sigmoid BCE,grouped-tie AP and hand confusion examples precede full ResNet checks,actual COCO128 image/support previews,visible SGD priors and complete-model Adam. Paired BN restoration,validation-only cutoffs and every held-out decision bitmap remain explicit.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.8_other_vision_tasks/multilabel_classification.cpp`.

> The method

Predict80 independent category-presence bits,weight rare positive fitting targets,and optimize explicit Bernoulli BCE. Keep official source annotations distinct from the custom80/24/24 split,group ranking ties,and select checkpoints and global cutoffs using separate validation images.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/multilabel_classification_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/multilabel_classification_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/multilabel_classification_concept.tikz > build/multilabel_classification_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/multilabel_classification_concept.svg build/multilabel_classification_concept.dvi > build/multilabel_classification_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
