> Independent category bits need independent sigmoids

A photograph may contain several categories. Its target is an80-bit presence
vector,not one mutually exclusive class. For one logit z and target y,stable
Bernoulli cross entropy is \(\ell=\operatorname{softplus}(z)-yz\).
Fitting-only positive factors w_c give

$$L=\frac1{NC}\sum_{i,c}[1+(w_c-1)y_{ic}]\ell(z_{ic},y_{ic}),\qquad
\frac{\partial L}{\partial z_{ic}}=\frac{[1+(w_c-1)y_{ic}](\sigma(z_{ic})-y_{ic})}{NC}.$$
\alttext(Independent sigmoid BCE weights only positive target bits by a per-class factor and averages over all image/category bits.)

The denominator stays N*C;it is not the sum of weights. The zero-logit
derivative is exactly weight_factor*(.5-y)/(N*C). Native independent oracles
check every weighted derivative at zero and logits +/-1000. Sigmoid outputs
need not sum to one. The illustration uses one category with positive weight3;
its per-bit derivative is recovered by multiplying the mean-loss gradient by
121 sample logits. No fitting occurs in this controlled example.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/multilabel_classification_objective.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  auto z = n::linspace(-6, 6, 121).requires_grad_();
  const auto positive = 3. * m::SiameseBinaryCrossEntropy(z, n::ones_like(z)),
             negative = m::SiameseBinaryCrossEntropy(z, n::zeros_like(z));
  const auto objective =
      m::MultilabelObjective(z.reshape({121, 1}), n::ones({121, 1}), n::tensor({3.}));
  const auto derivative = n::grad(objective, {z})[0] * 121.;
  if (std::abs(derivative.to_vector<float>()[60] + 1.5) > 1e-6)
    return 1;
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.lines(z.to_vector<double>(), positive.to_vector<double>(), "positive,w3", {37, 99, 235})
      .lines(z.to_vector<double>(), negative.to_vector<double>(), "negative,w1", {220, 38, 38})
      .title("Positive-only weighted bit BCE")
      .x_label("one category logit")
      .y_label("per-bit weighted loss")
      .y_limits(0, 23);
  b.lines(z.to_vector<double>(), derivative.to_vector<double>(), "positive gradient",
          {22, 163, 74})
      .title("Weighted positive logit derivative")
      .x_label("one category logit")
      .y_label("3*(sigmoid(z)-1)")
      .y_limits(-3.5, .5);
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/multilabel_classification_objective.svg");
  std::print("Positive factor3;zero-logit per-bit gradient-1.5. Mean weighted objective "
             "{:.6f};native every-logit extreme/zero derivative checks pass.\n",
             objective.item());
}
```
