> Full and compact80-logit ResNets execute

A small-stem ResNet18 retains eight residual blocks,global average pooling
and a biased80-logit head. Full widths have11,209,872 learned scalars plus
9,600 BN moving scalars. Compact widths divided by8 have180,952 learned
scalars plus1,200 BN moving scalars. Both have62 learned tensors and40 moving
moment tensors. The following block executes full and compact forward/backward
passes at64px;the compact check requires every learned tensor and RGB gradient
to be nonzero. BN uses old-value retention.9. There is no pretraining or dropout.

```{cpp, results="markdown", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;
  n::set_num_threads(2);
  for (int divisor : {1, 8}) {
    n::ParameterStore p(251), state(257);
    auto rgb = (.5 + .4 * n::sin(n::arange(0, 2 * 64 * 64 * 3).reshape({2, 64, 64, 3}) * .17))
                   .requires_grad_();
    const auto net = m::ResNet(p, state, rgb - .5, m::MultilabelConfig(divisor), true);
    auto variables = p.parameters();
    variables.push_back(rgb);
    const auto gradient = n::grad(n::mean(n::square(net.logits)), variables);
    if (p.count() != (divisor == 1 ? 11209872 : 180952) ||
        state.count() != (divisor == 1 ? 9600 : 1200) || p.size() != 62 ||
        state.size() != 40 || gradient.size() != 63 || net.blocks.size() != 8)
      return 1;
    for (const auto &g : gradient)
      if (!g.defined() || !std::isfinite(n::norm(g).item()) ||
          (divisor == 8 && n::norm(g).item() <= 0))
        return 1;
    std::print("{} ResNet18:{} learned/{} moving scalars;62 finite parameter gradients plus "
               "RGB,40 moving tensors,8 residual blocks,80 independent logits.\n",
               divisor == 1 ? "Full" : "Compact", p.count(), state.count());
  }
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Full ResNet18:11209872 learned/9600 moving scalars;62 finite parameter gradients plus RGB,40 moving tensors,8 residual blocks,80 independent logits.
Compact ResNet18:180952 learned/1200 moving scalars;62 finite parameter gradients plus RGB,40 moving tensors,8 residual blocks,80 independent logits.
// result_end

> Prepare and inspect actual COCO128 annotation-presence data

COCO128 supplies128 original COCO train2017 photographs and YOLO-style category
annotations. This report uses a reproducible **custom**80/24/24 split:sort
original image IDs,shuffle metadata with Python Random(271),then take80 fit,
24 validation and24 test rows. These are not official COCO evaluation splits.
The source archive fingerprint,selected IDs and category sets are recorded in
`manifest.json`;the preparation command may select different rows from an old
external `multilabel.npz`.

```{cpp, flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  const std::filesystem::path cache = dm::datasets::data_home();
  dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("multilabel", (cache / "multilabel").string());
}
```
// result_begin:
// result_end

Run preparation from the repository root after building the library(or use its
installed pkg-config entry). Python handles source files and integer category/ID
metadata. C++ decodes bytes;all grayscale-to-RGB conversion,division by255,
bilinear64px square stretching and category one-hot OR use the tensor library.
There is no crop,antialias filter,augmentation or box-coordinate processing.
Repeated same-category boxes still set one bit. Set `DATAMUNGE_MULTILABEL_DIR`
to use another prepared directory.

The pinned archive has no label files for image IDs250 and508. Following the
source loader convention,their category sets are empty;the manifest records
this explicitly. They fall in fitting and validation respectively. Two label
files without corresponding photographs are unused. Targets describe
**annotation presence**;missing bits do not prove visual absence,and a tiny
annotated object may become hard to see at64px.

Positive factors use only fitting labels:
\(w_c=\operatorname{clip}((N-pos_c+1)/(pos_c+1),1,20)\).
Absent fitting classes receive a finite capped factor,but this cannot create
positive examples. The actual first eight fitting photographs accompany the
full80-category support/weight profiles.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/multilabel_classification_balance.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>

#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  namespace m = n::models;

  std::filesystem::path cache;
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_DATA_DIR"))
    cache = p;
  else if (const auto *p = std::getenv("XDG_CACHE_HOME"))
    cache = std::filesystem::path(p) / "datamunge/datasets";
  else
    cache = std::filesystem::path(std::getenv("HOME")) / ".cache/datamunge/datasets";

  std::filesystem::path root = cache / "multilabel";
  if (const auto *p = std::getenv("DATAMUNGE_MULTILABEL_DIR"))
    root = p;
  else
    dm::datasets::prepare_example_data("multilabel", root.string());

  const auto data = m::LoadMultilabel(root);
  const auto support = n::count_nonzero(n::equal(data.fit.labels, 1.), {0}),
             weights = m::MultilabelWeights(data.fit.labels);
  const auto x = n::arange(0, 80).to_vector<double>();
  const auto per_image = n::count_nonzero(n::equal(data.fit.labels, 1.), {1})
                             .to_vector<std::int64_t>(),
             ids = data.fit.ids.to_vector<std::int64_t>();
  std::print("| first fitting image ID | annotated category count |\n|---:|---:|\n");
  for (int i = 0; i < 8; ++i)
    std::print("| {} | {} |\n", ids[i], per_image[i]);
  std::print("80/24/24 distinct image rows;{} fitting categories present,{} absent. "
             "Fitting-only weights in[{:.3f},{:.3f}].\n",
             n::count_nonzero(n::greater(support, 0.)).item<std::int64_t>(),
             n::count_nonzero(n::equal(support, 0.)).item<std::int64_t>(),
             n::min(weights).item(), n::max(weights).item());
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::filesystem::create_directories("figures");
  n::save_image_grid(n::slice_axis(data.fit.rgb, 0, 0, 8),
                     "build/multilabel_classification_data.png", 2, 0, 1, 3, 1, 3);
  std::filesystem::copy_file("build/multilabel_classification_data.png",
                             "figures/multilabel_classification_data.png",
                             std::filesystem::copy_options::overwrite_existing);
  auto a = dm::graphics::RPlot::create(), b = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
  a.bars(x, support.to_vector<double>(), "fitting images", {37, 99, 235}, .8)
      .title("Actual fitting category support")
      .x_label("COCO128 category0..79")
      .y_label("images with an annotation")
      .y_limits(0, 1.25 * n::max(support).item());
  b.bars(x, weights.to_vector<double>(), "positive factor", {217, 119, 6}, .8)
      .title("Fitting-only capped positive weights")
      .x_label("COCO128 category0..79")
      .y_label("weighted BCE positive factor")
      .y_limits(0, 25);
  auto layout = dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1, 2);
  layout.add(a).add(b).size(1100, 480).fit_panels().save_svg(
      "build/multilabel_classification_balance.svg");
}
