\caption(Thirty visible complete-model Adam updates with fitting-only positive factors. Paired learned/BN checkpoints select unweighted validation BCE;validation mAP is reported separately and does not select the checkpoint.)
\alttext(Thirty visible complete-model Adam updates with fitting-only positive factors. Paired learned/BN checkpoints select unweighted validation BCE;validation mAP is reported separately and does not select the checkpoint.)

\image(figures/multilabel_classification_metrics.svg)
\caption(Held-out present-class mAP and thresholded micro F1 compare learned CNN,untrained initialization,SGD-fitted constant prior and all-negative reference. Model cutoffs are chosen on validation. Constant/all-zero scores have prevalence AP because ties are grouped;this is distinct from predicting positive bits.)
\alttext(Held-out class-ranking and threshold-decision comparisons,including the constant prior and all-negative references.)

\image(figures/multilabel_classification_predictions.png)
\caption(All24 actual held-out photographs,two image tiles per row. Each tile is observed64px image,truth bitmap,decision bitmap. Bits follow COCO128 category order0–79,row-major in8x10 cells. Truth is bright/dark green;decisions are green TP,red FP,yellow FN,gray TN. Gaps are black;nearest scaling preserves cell geometry.)
\alttext(Actual held-out COCO photographs with independent annotation bits and calibrated positive/negative decision errors.)

The calibrated CNN reaches test mAP .184866 versus .072368 for the constant
prior, but its micro F1 .061538 is below the prior's .311111. Calibration
also lowers test F1 from the fixed-.5 CNN's .074074. Ranking and thresholded
decisions measure different properties, and the tiny validation split does
not guarantee transfer of its chosen cutoff.

A short weighted fit can improve the training objective while leaving weak
held-out probabilities and threshold decisions. Validation calibration does not
guarantee improved test F1. The printed present/absent supports,full confusion
counts and fitted-prior reference make class imbalance and generalization
limits visible. These custom annotation-presence results are not an official
COCO benchmark or a claim that every unannotated object is absent.

> Conclusion

Independent sigmoid targets,weighted gradients and score-group AP are inspectable before fitting. Actual images,explicit data preparation,visible SGD/Adam and paired-state deployment keep the small experiment reproducible. The full held-out comparison exposes the limits of a short weighted fit and the strength of simple class priors.

> References

- [Lin et al.(2014),Microsoft COCO:Common Objects in Context](https://arxiv.org/abs/1405.0312).
- [Ultralytics COCO128 source,category order and download](https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/blob/main/ultralytics/cfg/datasets/coco128.yaml).
- [Source loader’s missing-label convention](https://github.com/ultralytics/ultralytics/blob/main/ultralytics/data/utils.py).
- [Scikit-learn official noninterpolated average precision definition](https://scikit-learn.org/stable/modules/generated/sklearn.metrics.average_precision_score.html).
- [He et al.(2016),Deep Residual Learning for Image Recognition](https://arxiv.org/abs/1512.03385).
> Aggregated label confusion

This native SVG replots the calibrated CNN's recorded TP/FP/FN/TN counts in the
table above. Its 1920 observations are all 24 images times 80 labels, with absent
and present as the two classes. It summarizes binary label decisions; the per-label
AP and image-level metrics above retain their separate meanings. No model is refit.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/multilabel_classification_confusion_api_0.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
int main() {
  namespace n = dm::nn;
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto counts = n::from_vector(std::vector<std::int64_t>{1731, 123, 60, 6}, {2, 2});
  const auto matrix = n::ConfusionMatrix::from_counts(counts);
  if (std::abs(matrix.per_class(1).f1 - 0.061538) > 1e-6)
    return 1;
  matrix.save_svg(
      "build/multilabel_classification_confusion_api_0.svg",
      {.title     = "Calibrated CNN / all 1920 image-label decisions",
       .labels    = {"absent", "present"},
       .cell_size = 72,
       .font_size = 13});
  std::print("Recorded 1920 binary decisions; positive micro F1 {:.6f}.\n", matrix.per_class(1).f1);
}
